ore unchanged\", \"K2 unchanged\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6626}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6746}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3147}, \"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3296}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4000}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.4678, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 correct; geomean 1.0809x -> 1.4678x (+35.8%), the single largest jump so far, confirming prediction P1 (GEMMs dominate, tile policy is the primary lever). WL3 recovered from 0.889x to 1.315x. New current best-correct. Next: Phase C (fuse/tile the memory-bound K2) since GEMM tuning is largely captured; small-M cases (WL1/2 at ~1.66x) now lead, large-M (WL3/4 ~1.32x) lag -> remaining headroom is intermediate-traffic + launch overhead reduction.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}","originalFile":"{\"candidate_id\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"5e94b0ce7a6b56c81c5af357a9f9b38d07cb8c92a93d7393fcce70156e478cff\", \"hypothesis\": \"Correctness anchor: 3-kernel Triton decomposition (K1 GEMM1+bias, K2 fused gating+causal depthwise conv+gating, K3 GEMM2+bias) entirely in (M,H) row-major space, eliminating the reference's two transposes and .contiguous() copy; fp32 middle; single conservative tile (64x64x32, warps=4, stages=3). Goal: pass all 5 workloads and read the Triton-vs-cuBLAS GEMM gap.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"initial baseline\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"chunk offsets Bgate[0,H)/Cgate[H,2H)/Xproj[2H,3H)\", \"conv cross-correlation tap: k=3=current, d=(KC-1)-k\", \"causal+batch-boundary mask s>=d\", \"F.linear W^T\", \"fp32 GEMM+conv accum, bf16 store\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.1672}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.1714}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8887}, \"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.0255}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.1842}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.0809, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 workloads correct; baseline geomean 1.0809x. WL3 (M=8192, B=32,S=256) at 0.8887x is the weak point: conservative 64x64x32 tile underperforms cuBLAS at large M, confirming prediction P1 (GEMM tuning highest leverage). Set as current best-correct.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 1, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":1,"newStart":1,"newLines":2,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"5e94b0ce7a6b56c81c5af357a9f9b38d07cb8c92a93d7393fcce70156e478cff\", \"hypothesis\": \"Correctness anchor: 3-kernel Triton decomposition (K1 GEMM1+bias, K2 fused gating+causal depthwise conv+gating, K3 GEMM2+bias) entirely in (M,H) row-major space, eliminating the reference's two transposes and .contiguous() copy; fp32 middle; single conservative tile (64x64x32, warps=4, stages=3). Goal: pass all 5 workloads and read the Triton-vs-cuBLAS GEMM gap.\", \"change_vs_parent\": \"initial baseline\", \"validation\": {\"analytical_checks\": [\"chunk offsets Bgate[0,H)/Cgate[H,2H)/Xproj[2H,3H)\", \"conv cross-correlation tap: k=3=current, d=(KC-1)-k\", \"causal+batch-boundary mask s>=d\", \"F.linear W^T\", \"fp32 GEMM+conv accum, bf16 store\"], \"expected_correct\": true}, \"results\": {\"b0a9e3f0\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1