\"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6626}, \"8b678b13\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 4, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.6746}, \"58e3ac47\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 32, \"S\": 256}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3147}, \"6033fd0f\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 2, \"S\": 4096}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.3296}, \"bb262a64\": {\"axes\": {\"B\": 1, \"S\": 2048}, \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.4000}}, \"geomean_speedup\": 1.4678, \"all_correct\": true, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"All 5 correct; geomean 1.0809x -> 1.4678x (+35.8%), the single largest jump so far, confirming prediction P1 (GEMMs dominate, tile policy is the primary lever). WL3 recovered from 0.889x to 1.315x. New current best-correct. Next: Phase C (fuse/tile the memory-bound K2) since GEMM tuning is largely captured; small-M cases (WL1/2 at ~1.66x) now lead, large-M (WL3/4 ~1.32x) lag -> remaining headroom is intermediate-traffic + launch overhead reduction.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"none (KernelWiki N/A for sm_80; profiler disallowed)\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
